### ÉTAPE 2 : TEST CAMELCASE - GET Peripherals
### ====================================

### 2.1 - Récupérer les périphériques (format camelCase attendu)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Devices/{{deviceId}}/peripherals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
# ✅ VÉRIFICATION ATTENDUE:
# {
#   "name": "led_rdc",        // ✅ camelCase (PAS "Name")
#   "gpio": 27,               // ✅ camelCase (PAS "Gpio")
#   "isOutput": true,         // ✅ camelCase (PAS "IsOutput")
#   "activeHigh": true,       // ✅ camelCase (PAS "ActiveHigh")
#   "ratedWatt": 5,           // ✅ camelCase (PAS "RatedWatt")
#   "wiringDiagram": null     // ✅ camelCase (PAS "WiringDiagram")
# }

### ====================================
### ÉTAPE 3 : TEST CAMELCASE - PUT Configuration
### ====================================

### 3.1 - Envoyer configuration en camelCase
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/Devices/{{deviceId}}/peripherals
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "peripherals": [
    {
      "id": "led-test-001",
      "name": "led_test",
      "type": "light",
      "gpio": 27,
      "notes": "LED test camelCase",
      "unit": "W",
      "metering": "estimated",
      "ratedWatt": 5,
      "isOutput": true,
      "activeHigh": true
    }
  ]
}

###
# ✅ VÉRIFICATION ATTENDUE:
# - Le backend accepte le JSON en camelCase
# - Les données sont envoyées à IoT Hub en camelCase
# - La réponse est en camelCase

### ====================================
### ÉTAPE 4 : TEST CAMELCASE - Device Twin
